target:    readme.txt
gate:      php tests/db-floor-metadata-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    but ADR-2's floor is
rationale: Put the 5.0.3 claim back. It is impossible on its face - the schema creates utf8mb4 tables and utf8mb4 landed in MySQL 5.5.3 - and readme.txt contradicted it 100 lines later by saying the floor is tested at 5.6/5.7/8.0. Two numbers in one file, and whichever a user read was a coin flip.
---
--- a/readme.txt
+++ b/readme.txt
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
 = Requirements =
 * WordPress 5.6+
 * PHP 7.4+
-* MySQL 5.6+ (or MariaDB 10.0+)
+* MySQL 5.0.3+
 * At least 5 MB of free web space (240 MB if you plan on using the external libraries for geolocation and browser detection)
 * At least 10 MB of free DB space
 * At least 32 Mb of free PHP memory for the tracker (peak memory usage)
